ctrl shift P -> user settings.json

add the following

    "vim.handleKeys": {
    "<C-a>": false,
    "<C-p>": false,
    "<C-f>": false,
    // VS Code new marker @ next occurrence
    "<C-d>": false,
    // Copy
    "<C-c>": false,
    // Cut
    "<C-x>": false,
    // Paste
    "<C-v>": false,
    "<C-z>": false,
    "<C-y>": false,
},


ctrl shift P => Open Keyboard Shortcuts (JSON)

[
    // Navigate Splits
    {
        "key": "ctrl+h",
        "command": "workbench.action.navigateLeft"
    },
    {
        "key": "ctrl+l",
        "command": "workbench.action.navigateRight"
    },
    {
        "key": "ctrl+k",
        "command": "workbench.action.navigateUp"
    },
    {
        "key": "ctrl+j",
        "command": "workbench.action.navigateDown"
    }


    // Navigate buffers
    {
        "key": "ctrl+m",
        "command": "workbench.action.previousEditor"
    },
    {
        "key": "ctrl+n",
        "command": "workbench.action.nextEditor"
    }
]
